{"name":"Trillium","hex":"#a89896","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Trillium","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A taxonomic genus within the family Melanthiaceae."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Trillium"}],"entries":[{"title":"Trillium","blocks":[{"text":"Trillium is a genus of about fifty flowering plant species in the family Melanthiaceae. Trillium species are native to temperate regions of North America and Asia, with the greatest diversity of species found in the southern Appalachian Mountains in the southeastern United States."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/df/TrilliumErectum.jpg/330px-TrilliumErectum.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Trillium"},{"title":"Trillium (opera cycle)","blocks":[{"text":"Trillium is an ongoing opera cycle being composed by Anthony Braxton. The cycle is planned to consist of 12 operas, each comprising 1 to 5 acts that can be performed in any order by ensembles of varying size. Each opera explores different philosophical frameworks developed by Braxton in his Tri-Axium Writings."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4a/Anthony_Braxton_%28Speaking_Portraits%29_%28Vol._I%29.jpg/330px-Anthony_Braxton_%28Speaking_Portraits%29_%28Vol._I%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Trillium_(opera_cycle)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a2/Trillium_grandiflorum_at_the_North_Walker_Woods1.jpg/500px-Trillium_grandiflorum_at_the_North_Walker_Woods1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a2/Trillium_grandiflorum_at_the_North_Walker_Woods1.jpg/1280px-Trillium_grandiflorum_at_the_North_Walker_Woods1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parse